  id: methane-combustion
  title: Methane combustion
  equation: CH4 + 2 O2 -> CO2 + 2 H2O
  requiredCondition: 1
  reversible: 0
  conditions: Ignition and sufficient oxygen for complete combustion
  sources:
  - https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/4-1-writing-and-balancing-chemical-equations
  explanation: Complete combustion forms carbon dioxide and water. Oxygen limitation can produce other products; those pathways and heat are not simulated.
